WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.750
We want to know what
an update rule changes,

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:08.530
so we avoid a large cross product in
which many settings move together.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:12.310
The optimizer family fixes
batch size thirty two.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:16.810
The batch family fixes SGD
and rate zero point zero one.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.210
The schedule family fixes SGD, batch
thirty two and its selected starting rate.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.470
They share the same calendar inputs,
training only scaler,

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:29.450
zero weights and mean bias,

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.530
frozen row identities
and error definitions.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:35.030
The three seeds are seventeen,

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:36.910
twenty nine and forty three.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:41.370
Matching a seed pairs the training
order across comparable trials.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:44.770
These controls make a measured
difference interpretable.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:48.790
They do not remove the additive
model limitations already observed.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:52.470
Before the main trials,

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:57.290
each rule receives the same four candidate
rates and two hundred pilot updates.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.990
We reset parameters and
optimizer buffers each time.

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:06.490
Selection uses final full training half
squared error among completed candidates.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.390
Validation has not been loaded.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:11.810
SGD chooses zero point zero one,

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:16.050
momentum zero point zero zero one,
and Adam one.

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:19.167
Their selected training losses
are about three thousand,

00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:20.590
two hundred and seventy two,

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:22.850
three thousand,
two hundred and fifty five,

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:24.870
and three thousand,
two hundred and fifty six.

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:29.670
Rate one makes the SGD and
momentum pilots diverge.

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:32.830
Those failures are retained,
rather than erased from the allowance.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.850
We then write and hash the selected rates,

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.790
budgets and seeds before
fitting main trials.

00:01:41.025 --> 00:01:45.215
This shortened source trace makes
the information boundary visible.

00:01:45.565 --> 00:01:50.325
Training pilots determine the rates,
and a saved protocol fixes those choices.

00:01:50.325 --> 00:01:54.735
Main fitting finishes
before validation is loaded.

00:01:55.425 --> 00:01:57.475
The shared scorer then checks record,

00:01:57.845 --> 00:02:00.055
target time and issue time alignment.

00:02:01.165 --> 00:02:04.175
The rate one failures retain
explicit work counters.

00:02:04.845 --> 00:02:09.185
A failed attempted batch can consume
examples without completing another

00:02:09.185 --> 00:02:10.315
parameter update.

00:02:10.945 --> 00:02:16.015
The failure record therefore distinguishes
examples visited from updates applied.

00:02:16.605 --> 00:02:19.365
A failed pilot is retained
as evidence about its rate,

00:02:19.365 --> 00:02:21.795
without receiving a validation score.

00:02:23.918 --> 00:02:29.368
Identical configurations reuse the
same fitted trial for a given seed.

00:02:29.978 --> 00:02:34.408
There are twelve pilot candidates
and eighteen unique main fits.

00:02:35.138 --> 00:02:40.368
Reused SGD entries are not
extra independent repetitions,

00:02:40.458 --> 00:02:43.688
even when they appear in
more than one family table.

00:02:44.198 --> 00:02:49.238
A small integration fixture changes
validation outcomes and checks that pilot

00:02:49.238 --> 00:02:52.488
choices and saved model
bytes remain unchanged.

00:02:53.278 --> 00:02:58.048
Independent audits also recalculate
protocol and artifact hashes,

00:02:58.258 --> 00:03:00.708
training work counts,
prediction identities

00:03:01.198 --> 00:03:02.208
and scalar metrics.

00:03:03.318 --> 00:03:06.158
These checks support the
declared information boundary,

00:03:06.158 --> 00:03:10.048
while the later validation
scores measure forecast behavior.

00:03:12.275 --> 00:03:14.885
At batch thirty two and ten passes,

00:03:15.435 --> 00:03:20.055
mean validation absolute error is one
hundred and sixteen point one seven for

00:03:20.055 --> 00:03:20.925
SGD,

00:03:21.475 --> 00:03:24.245
one hundred and sixteen
point six zero for momentum,

00:03:24.855 --> 00:03:27.925
and one hundred and fourteen
point three six for Adam.

00:03:28.395 --> 00:03:33.405
Adam has the lowest observed mean, but its
sample deviation is two point three seven,

00:03:33.795 --> 00:03:37.365
larger than the roughly zero
point six for the other rules.

00:03:37.955 --> 00:03:42.005
All remain worse than the group
baseline at ninety one point five seven.

00:03:42.735 --> 00:03:46.265
Three orderings provide a small
reproducibility comparison,

00:03:46.795 --> 00:03:48.925
not a population confidence interval.

00:03:49.535 --> 00:03:54.365
Pilot seed seventeen is also one
main seed, which we declare openly.

00:03:55.015 --> 00:03:59.695
We retain every seed result and avoid
presenting the most flattering one as the

00:03:59.695 --> 00:04:00.565
whole experiment.

00:04:02.793 --> 00:04:05.723
Return to the later Monday at eight.

00:04:06.213 --> 00:04:08.723
Its target is four hundred
and twenty rentals.

00:04:09.673 --> 00:04:10.803
For seed seventeen,

00:04:11.213 --> 00:04:15.103
SGD forecasts one hundred and
sixty eight point nine one,

00:04:15.233 --> 00:04:19.043
while Adam forecasts one hundred
and fifty three point two one.

00:04:19.613 --> 00:04:25.063
Adam is worse on this hour even though
its overall mean absolute error is lower.

00:04:25.973 --> 00:04:28.743
Average improvement is not a
promise for every observation.

00:04:29.713 --> 00:04:33.913
Both rules still produce negative
predictions at the quiet two oclock

00:04:33.913 --> 00:04:34.523
example.

00:04:35.173 --> 00:04:38.763
We keep raw predictions without
hidden clipping or rounding.

00:04:39.373 --> 00:04:43.463
The optimizer changes the route through
the same additive function family;

00:04:43.573 --> 00:04:46.923
it cannot invent an hour
by working day interaction.

00:04:47.893 --> 00:04:50.523
The measured outcome supports
a bounded comparison,

00:04:50.993 --> 00:04:55.343
while the stronger group baseline and
remaining forecast failures stay visible.

